WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.037
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.839
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:15.008
Unit thirteen: Cultural Exchange. Today you will make wishes with 'wish' + past simple.

4
00:00:15.308 --> 00:00:17.948
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.133
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:24.495
Exchange program.

7
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:29.364
Exchange program means a plan where students study in another country.

8
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.507
She went to Japan on an exchange program.

9
00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:36.059
Your turn. Say: Exchange program.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.574
Exchange program.

11
00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:42.480
Host family.

12
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:46.655
Host family means a family that lets a visitor live with them.

13
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.238
My host family taught me to cook.

14
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.491
Your turn. Say: Host family.

15
00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:56.590
Host family.

16
00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:58.688
Cultural immersion.

17
00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:03.053
Cultural immersion means living fully inside another culture.

18
00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:06.787
Cultural immersion is the fastest way to learn.

19
00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:10.152
Your turn. Say: Cultural immersion.

20
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.419
Cultural immersion.

21
00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:16.695
Language exchange.

22
00:01:17.683 --> 00:01:21.424
Language exchange means two people teaching each other their languages.

23
00:01:22.017 --> 00:01:24.806
I do a language exchange with a French student.

24
00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:28.359
Your turn. Say: Language exchange.

25
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.921
Language exchange.

26
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:35.044
Global perspective.

27
00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:39.211
Global perspective means understanding the world as a whole.

28
00:01:39.817 --> 00:01:42.037
Travel gives you a global perspective.

29
00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:45.848
Your turn. Say: Global perspective.

30
00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.409
Global perspective.

31
00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.325
Tolerance.

32
00:01:53.317 --> 00:01:56.617
Tolerance means accepting views that are different from yours.

33
00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.309
Tolerance makes friendship possible.

34
00:01:59.917 --> 00:02:02.418
Your turn. Say: Tolerance.

35
00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:06.256
Tolerance.

36
00:02:07.017 --> 00:02:08.981
Diversity appreciation.

37
00:02:09.983 --> 00:02:13.759
Diversity appreciation means valuing differences between people.

38
00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:17.011
Our festival builds diversity appreciation.

39
00:02:17.617 --> 00:02:20.838
Your turn. Say: Diversity appreciation.

40
00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.560
Diversity appreciation.

41
00:02:26.317 --> 00:02:27.921
Cross-cultural friendship.

42
00:02:28.917 --> 00:02:32.983
Cross-cultural friendship means friendship between people of different cultures.

43
00:02:33.583 --> 00:02:36.547
My cross-cultural friendship with Yuki is special.

44
00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:40.511
Your turn. Say: Cross-cultural friendship.

45
00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.239
Cross-cultural friendship.

46
00:02:45.983 --> 00:02:46.741
Custom.

47
00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.446
Custom means a traditional way of doing something.

48
00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.630
Taking off shoes indoors is a Khmer custom.

49
00:02:54.217 --> 00:02:56.602
Your turn. Say: Custom.

50
00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:00.294
Custom.

51
00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:01.935
Etiquette.

52
00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.472
Etiquette means the rules of polite behaviour.

53
00:03:06.083 --> 00:03:08.512
Learn the table etiquette before you visit.

54
00:03:09.117 --> 00:03:11.444
Your turn. Say: Etiquette.

55
00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.197
Etiquette.

56
00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.404
Broaden horizons.

57
00:03:18.417 --> 00:03:21.345
Broaden horizons means to learn about new things.

58
00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:23.903
Reading broadens your horizons.

59
00:03:24.517 --> 00:03:27.982
Your turn. Say: Broaden horizons.

60
00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:32.415
Broaden horizons.

61
00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:33.989
Empathy.

62
00:03:34.983 --> 00:03:37.656
Empathy means understanding how others feel.

63
00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.017
Living abroad builds empathy.

64
00:03:40.617 --> 00:03:43.223
Your turn. Say: Empathy.

65
00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:46.905
Empathy.

66
00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:51.722
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:52.583 --> 00:03:55.999
Visal, what would you like to learn from a cultural exchange program?

68
00:03:57.083 --> 00:04:01.257
I wish I could join one! I'd love to learn Japanese customs.

69
00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:04.083
Do you speak Japanese?

70
00:04:05.183 --> 00:04:10.810
Not yet. I wish I knew more languages. I'm doing a language exchange online.

71
00:04:11.917 --> 00:04:13.382
What else would you learn?

72
00:04:14.483 --> 00:04:20.386
Etiquette, tolerance and empathy. I wish I had a host family in Kyoto!

73
00:04:21.533 --> 00:04:22.987
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:26.813
Grammar focus: wish plus past simple.

75
00:04:27.113 --> 00:04:28.381
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:29.083 --> 00:04:31.640
I wish I could join an exchange program.

77
00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.642
I wish I knew more languages.

78
00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.944
She wishes she had a host family abroad.

79
00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:42.432
Use 'wish' + past simple for wishes about now that are not true.

80
00:04:43.183 --> 00:04:47.357
Be careful! Don't say: I wish I can join an exchange program.

81
00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.402
Say: I wish I could join an exchange program.

82
00:04:52.702 --> 00:04:56.153
After 'wish', use the past form: could, knew, had.

83
00:04:56.967 --> 00:04:59.654
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:01.595
A Year Abroad.

85
00:05:01.895 --> 00:05:04.696
My cousin lived with a host family in Australia.

86
00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.048
Cultural immersion broadened her horizons.

87
00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:12.577
Language exchange built empathy and cross-cultural friendship.

88
00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:16.147
She learned new customs and table etiquette.

89
00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.760
I wish I could join an exchange program too.

90
00:05:20.867 --> 00:05:24.938
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:25.783 --> 00:05:27.864
I wish I blank more languages.

92
00:05:28.164 --> 00:05:30.877
A, knew. B, know. C, known.

93
00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:35.818
The answer is A: knew.

94
00:05:36.983 --> 00:05:40.341
A family that lets a visitor live with them is a blank family.

95
00:05:40.641 --> 00:05:44.132
A, host. B, guest. C, exchange.

96
00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:49.446
The answer is A: host.

97
00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.641
The rules of polite behaviour are blank.

98
00:05:52.941 --> 00:05:56.606
A, etiquette. B, customs. C, tolerance.

99
00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:02.120
The answer is A: etiquette.

100
00:06:03.333 --> 00:06:06.497
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:10.325
What would you like to learn from a cultural exchange program?

102
00:06:19.117 --> 00:06:20.733
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:28.596
I would like to learn how people live and think in another country. I wish I could stay with a host family and learn their language.

104
00:06:28.896 --> 00:06:30.699
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:31.583 --> 00:06:35.838
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and wish plus past simple.

106
00:06:36.138 --> 00:06:41.495
Today's value is open-mindedness. Be open to new places, people and ideas.

107
00:06:41.795 --> 00:06:44.285
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:44.585 --> 00:06:48.062
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

